description: Project standards for React Router, Prisma, GitHub, and frontend code
alwaysApply: true

---

# Project Standards

- Use React Router 7 as the application framework and follow its conventions for routes, loaders, actions, and server/client boundaries.
- Never import `*.server` modules for values used in a route's default component or other client exports; put shared constants/helpers in non-`.server` files. `npm run build` catches this; lint/typecheck do not.
- Use Prisma as the ORM for database access and prefer Prisma-based solutions over introducing other data access layers unless the user asks for it.
- For GitHub work, treat this `mealplanner` project as the default repository context unless the user explicitly points to another repository.
- Default to React, TypeScript, and Tailwind solutions that are clean, concise, and easy to maintain.
- Prefer extending or extracting reusable components, hooks, and helpers over duplicating UI or logic.
- Keep components focused; move complex state, data shaping, or conditional rendering into small helpers when it improves clarity.
- Favor clear prop APIs and strong typing over broad, hard-to-maintain abstractions.
- Reuse existing primitives and patterns before introducing new wrappers, variants, or utilities.
- In Tailwind, prefer readable utility composition and shared patterns over long repeated class strings.
- Use `wrap-break-word` instead of `break-words`. Tailwind reports `The class break-words can be written as wrap-break-word`.
- Match existing project conventions and keep changes minimal.
- POST mutations must use React Router `<Form>` (or `useFetcher` / `useSubmit`), never a native `<form method="post">`. Action redirects must be relative via `redirect()` — never `new URL(path, request.url)`. See `.cursor/rules/react-router-form.mdc`.
- Client form submissions must update visible data immediately (optimistic). Pending-only `"Lagrer..."` is not enough; follow `.cursor/rules/optimistic-form-updates.mdc`.
- Text inputs (`input`, `textarea`, searchable fields) must use `text-base` (16px) or larger — never `text-sm`/`text-xs` — to prevent iOS Safari focus zoom. See `.cursor/rules/ios-input-font-size.mdc`.

## Brand palette

The Ukesstripe home design is the color source for the product. Use these tokens for shared chrome (page, cards, text, borders, primary actions). Do not introduce new slate, emerald, or one-off hex colors for that chrome.

Define them in `app/app.css` `@theme` when implementing the home page, then reuse the Tailwind colors (`bg-page`, `text-ink`, `bg-accent`, and so on). Light values replace the current slate scale (`#f1f5f9`, `#0f172a`, `#475569`, `#e2e8f0`).

| Token | Light | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--color-page` | `#f3f6f4` | Page background |
| `--color-surface` | `#ffffff` | Cards and panels |
| `--color-ink` | `#14211c` | Body text. It flips in dark mode, so do not use it as a hero background. |
| `--color-band` | `#14211c` | Dark heroes, closing bands, and the top bar. Dark mode lifts this to `#24352e`. |
| `--color-on-band` | `#f4faf7` | Text on `band` |
| `--color-on-band-muted` | `#c9d7d1` | Secondary text on `band` |
| `--color-on-band-quiet` | `#9fb2aa` | Quiet text on `band` |
| `--color-kicker` | `#9ee6db` | Eyebrow labels on `band` |
| `--color-muted` | `#5c6b64` | Secondary text |
| `--color-line` | `#d9e3dc` | Borders and dividers |
| `--color-accent` | `#0f766e` | Primary buttons and kickers |
| `--color-accent-strong` | `#115e59` | Primary hover |
| `--color-accent-soft` | `#d8f3ee` | Soft accent fills |
| `--color-paper` | `#fffdf8` | Warm illustrated cards |

Dark hero and closing band, on `--color-ink`:

| Role | Color |
| --- | --- |
| Text | `#f4faf7` |
| Secondary text | `#c9d7d1` |
| Quiet text | `#9fb2aa` |
| Kicker | `#9ee6db` |

Dark mode stays in this green-black family. Do not keep the slate dark scale (`#020617`, `#0f172a`, `#334155`). Page `#0e1915`, surface `#17241f`, ink `#f4faf7`, muted `#9fb2aa`, line `#314840`, accent-strong `#14b8a6` (lighter hover), accent-soft `#14332f`. Store-mode tokens (`--color-store-*`) use these same brand roles. Notice colors stay as they are.

Illustration-only colors, for flat drawings and not UI chrome: stroke `#1c2b24`, tomato `#e36b4f`, yolk `#f0c14d`, leaf `#3d9a78`, salmon `#f0a07a`, dough `#f3e2c4`, meat `#c46b4a`. Drawings stay clearly illustrated.

```tsx
type ButtonProps = React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> & {
  tone?: "primary" | "secondary";
};

export function Button({ tone = "primary", className, ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button className={cn(buttonStyles({ tone }), className)} {...props} />
  );
}
```
